## 📦 Environment & Dependencies (uv)

`uv` (Astral, Rust) is the environment + dependency manager — it replaces pip, venv, pyenv,
and pip-tools with one fast binary, and is the 2026 default (now past Poetry in downloads).
`pyproject.toml` is the single source of truth; **no `requirements.txt`**.

```bash
uv init                     # scaffold pyproject.toml
uv add pandas pydantic pydantic-settings structlog stamina   # runtime deps
uv add --dev pytest ruff mypy deepeval   # dev-only → [dependency-groups]
uv sync                     # reproduce the exact locked env on any machine
uv run pytest               # run inside the env (no manual activate)
```

- Commit `uv.lock` — it pins exact versions/hashes for reproducible installs.
- Dev tools go in `[dependency-groups]`, keeping runtime deps lean.
- `uv run <cmd>` auto-activates the env; no `source .venv/bin/activate` needed.

## 🔧 Tooling Configuration

> **2026 stack:** `uv` (env + deps) · `ruff` (lint + format + import sort) · `mypy` (types).
> This collapses pip/venv, Black, isort, and flake8 into two Rust binaries — one config file.

### Ruff (Linting + Formatting — replaces Black, isort, flake8)
```toml
# pyproject.toml
[tool.ruff]
target-version = "py312"
line-length = 88

[tool.ruff.lint]
select = [
    "E",    # pycodestyle errors
    "F",    # pyflakes
    "I",    # isort (import sorting)
    "W",    # pycodestyle warnings
    "UP",   # pyupgrade (modern Python syntax)
    "B",    # flake8-bugbear
    "SIM",  # flake8-simplify
]
ignore = ["E501"]  # line length handled by formatter

[tool.ruff.lint.isort]
known-first-party = ["src"]

[tool.ruff.format]
quote-style = "double"
```

### Formatting (`ruff format` — Black is retired)
`ruff format` is a drop-in Black replacement (~99.9% identical output, 10–100× faster) and
ships the "2026 style" in Ruff ≥ 0.15. **Do not run Black separately** — one tool, one config.
Import sorting is Ruff's `I` lint rule; no standalone `isort`.

### mypy (Type Checking)
```toml
[tool.mypy]
python_version = "3.12"
strict = false          # tighten to true as a project matures
warn_return_any = true
warn_unused_configs = true
```
> `ty` (Astral's fast type checker) is emerging and pairs with uv/ruff; mypy remains the
> reference implementation with the widest library compatibility — stay on mypy for now.

